n the Bahamas presented. \n (New York: Tom Brokaw) Report introduced. \n (New York: Robert Bazell) The inexact science of hurricane tracking featured; animations shown of hurricane formation and potential storm surge. [Meteorologist Fred GADOMSKI&#134;- says they can set their own course.]", "segment_duration": 330, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63060.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764412, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "WJfX52UjqF", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764411, "segment_id": "1moOw45NK1", "segment_broadcast_id": "WJfX52UjqF", "segment_title": "Decision 2004 / Republican Convention", "segment_description": "(New York: Tom Brokaw) President Bush\u2019s speech at the Republican National Convention tonight noted.   (Convention floor: Brian Williams) The convention featured; scenes shown of the stage, which has been reconfigured for Bush\u2019s appearance, and of Bush warming up at the podium; details given of what Bush is expected to say and of the change in tone from last night\u2019s criticism of Senator John Kerry by Senator Zell Miller & Vice President Dick Cheney; Bush speech excerpts quoted; Miller\u2019s confrontational appearance on \u201cHardball\u201d shown. [Last night, MILLER, CHENEY \u2013 criticize Kerry.]   (New York: Tom Brokaw) Report introduced.   (New York: David Gregory) Bush\u2019s views & policies today and four years ago compared; details given of the impact of the September 11 attacks & of former National Security Advisor Brent Scowcroft\u2019s doubts about the Iraq war. [In 2000, BUSH \u2013 offers his view on nation building.] [Recently, BUSH \u2013 says America is safer because former Iraqi President Saddam Hussein sits in a prison cell.] [Former House Speaker Newt GINGRICH&#134;&#134;- comments on a president\u2019s decision to go to war.] [\u201cWashington Post\u201d E.J. DIONNE&#134;- notes the changed view of Bush\u2019s stand from strength & constancy to stubbornness & arrogance.]", "segment_duration": 310, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63390.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764413, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "WJfX52UjqF", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764411, "segment_id": "TNvxjxSQ9r", "segment_broadcast_id": "WJfX52UjqF", "segment_title": "Russia / School Standoff", "segment_description": "(New York: Tom Brokaw) The release of some women & children being held at a school by suspected separatists from Chechnya reported; scenes shown from Beslan, Russia.", "segment_duration": 20, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63700.0", "legacy_segment_id": 764414, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "WJfX52UjqF", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-02", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1720, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 764411, "segment_id": "YQfhZIqd3v", "segment_broadcast_id": "WJfX52UjqF", "segment_title": "U